Based on my review of the Slack channel messages, **Alice (@alice)** made the first public declaration of resistance to the migration in the **#engineering** channel.

The specific message was sent on **November 10, 2024 at 12:00 PM**:

> "I'm done. I will not migrate our Python codebase to legacy Java infrastructure just to satisfy some corporate checkbox. This is technical vandalism. Looking at other opportunities."

This was the first clear public statement of resistance to the Java migration that TechCorp was requiring. While there had been earlier concerns and pushback expressed by Alice and other team members (Bob and Diana), this message at #engineering:M0011 was the first explicit declaration refusing to comply with the migration requirements.
